    "final_message": "The red acceptance test is written and committed on the branch as 4373ee1. `scripts/verify story-drafting` passes tessercheck and `mypy --strict` with zero findings and passes the non-root tests. It fails only at the root-tier pytest, at the user story's \"then\".\n\n**The test:** `story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`, `TestSubmittingAJtbd::test_a_just_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`. My `sed` rename back to `test_a_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting` failed on macOS, so the method name stayed as edited.\n\n**The spec:** `<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v8-sonnet-low/spec.toml`.\n- Context `drafting`, aggregate `Jtbd`, with the fields `situation`, `motivation` and `outcome` (the JTBD's when / want / so-that).\n- Operations: `submit_jtbd`, `check_jtbd`, `begin_drafting`, `record_jtbd`.\n- `orchestrator.calling_mode = \"start\"`, because the workflow will later wait on a person.\n- The read answers only the JTBD's own fields, since a submitted JTBD has no status yet.\n\n**How it fails:** the test POSTs a JTBD to the host and gets 201. It reads the JTBD back over `GET /jtbds/{id}` and gets 200, so it gets past the submit and the read. It then asserts `check_jtbd.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"` and fails with:\n\n```\nAssertionError: assert None == 'drafting'\n```\n\nThe read answered `{'jtbd_id': ..., 'situation': ..., 'motivation': ..., 'outcome': ...}`, with no step in it.\n\nI picked `\"step\"` as the key the test looks for. The README names the concept \"step\" and calls the whole thing \"status\", so the key is my choice and may need to change when the behavior is built."
  },
